  "tagging_policy": {
    "editing": "Edit publication-topics.csv: each keyword has its own column, with x for applicable keywords and blanks otherwise. Keep id, year, and title unchanged, then run python3 update-publication-topics.py to regenerate the JSON and browser data. Parent categories are included automatically.",
    "overlap": "Papers may have multiple tags. Tags describe central contributions, core techniques, or the systems being studied, rather than every ingredient used.",
    "inheritance": "Paper tags explicitly include declared parent tags, except per-paper excluded_parent_tags, so filters can use direct membership checks. Exclusions prevent automatic inheritance but do not override explicit CSV assignments.",
    "generative_models": "Umbrella for generative methods and work directly studying generative systems. GANs, diffusion, flow matching, and autoregressive generation imply this tag.",
    "responsible_genai": "Umbrella covering data attribution, detection/image forensics, and unlearning/concept erasure.",
    "interaction": "Human-directed controls or an explicitly interactive workflow; not simply attention or interaction between generated samples.",
    "topic_approval": "All listed topics are approved and may overlap. Topic origin records whether a topic came from the user or an assistant suggestion, not its approval status.",
    "personalization_customization_few_shot_generation": "Adapting generation to particular subjects, concepts, domains, styles, or motions, and learning generation from limited examples. These overlapping capabilities share one keyword.",
    "video_generation": "Includes video synthesis, video prediction, and world models.",
    "diffusion_flow_matching": "One keyword covers diffusion models, flow-matching models, and hybrid formulations.",
    "broad_modalities": "Image covers still-image generation, editing, analysis, and image-based geometry; Audio, Video, and Language retain their dedicated scopes. Modalities can overlap.",
    "understanding_models": "Discriminative prediction and analysis: recognition/classification, detection, segmentation, alignment/shape regression, learned similarity metrics, and representation learning intended for perception. Curated independently: a generative paper does not qualify merely because it uses a feature encoder, representation alignment, a vision-language model, or a GAN discriminator. May overlap with Generative models when discriminative learning or evaluation is a central contribution.",
    "distillation_efficiency": "Combines generative teacher-to-student distillation with central improvements to training or inference computation, memory, or latency. Includes few-step models; not synonymous with few-shot data efficiency.",
    "perceptual_metrics": "Combines perceptual models and evaluation metrics. Excludes Evaluating Data Attribution and Diffusion2GAN, whose main contributions are not metrics."
  },
